 "limits": [
  "one cell line and one growth condition per assay: ENCODE K562 is not the K562 the Perturb-seq screen was run in -- different laboratory, medium, passage. Cell-MATCHED here means the same immortalised line, not the same culture.",
  "RNA is polyA-plus only, so non-polyadenylated transcripts (replication-dependent histones, many lncRNAs) are systematically under-measured and their TPM is not a level, it is a floor.",
  "TPM is a steady-state level, not a synthesis rate: a short-lived transcript at the same TPM is being made far faster, and nothing here separates the two.",
  "promoter accessibility is a peak CALL within +/-1000 bp of one annotated TSS. Genes with multiple TSSs are scored at one of them, and a promoter with no peak is below the pipeline's threshold, not demonstrably closed.",
  "the ATAC signalValue is fold-enrichment against each experiment's own background and is NOT comparable across experiments; it is rank-normalised within experiment before combining, which preserves order and discards magnitude.",
  "this layer is a STATE, not a response. It says what K562 looks like unperturbed; it says nothing about how expression or accessibility MOVE after a perturbation.",
  "the layer is a per-gene covariate, not a link set, so the standard pair fast test cannot score it (Q5 shows the matching removes it by construction). Its value is measured as covariate quality and as its effect on an already-banked matched result.",
  "Williams' t is applied to Spearman coefficients, which is an approximation; the bootstrap over genes is the primary statistic for every predictor contest here.",
  "the decile match used by the standard fast test does not fully balance its own covariates at this sample size -- on the 213k PPI pairs it leaves a standardised difference of about 0.11 on gene responsiveness. That is a property of the reference test, inherited by every number compared against it here, and it is why residuals are reported as effect sizes as well as p-values.",
  "the perturbation-axis contest uses one GWPS row per perturbed gene, so it is not inflated by pseudo-replication; the gene-axis and PPI arms are not de-replicated and their p-values are correspondingly optimistic (the ratios and Spearman coefficients are not).",
  "the eight RNA experiments span 2011-2016 and five laboratories, and their median pairwise Spearman is about 0.86: the K562 expression value used here is a median over that spread, not a single measurement, and gene-level disagreement between laboratories is real and unmodelled."
 ],
 "verdict": "CELL-MATCHED RNA IS THE BETTER COVARIATE, ON BOTH AXES AND BY A MARGIN THAT SURVIVES RESAMPLING. Against gene responsiveness it reaches Spearman +0.329 where the generic `ppm` reaches +0.268 on the same 6,976 genes (K562 wins 100% of 2,000 gene bootstraps, delta|rho| +0.061 [+0.039, +0.084]); against perturbation strength +0.173 against +0.130 over 8,620 perturbed genes (100% of bootstraps). In raw held-out terms the top decile of K562 expression carries mean |z| 1.095 against 0.831 in the bottom (1.317x) where the generic table separates only 1.211x. The mechanism behind the second axis holds: perturbations of the 830 targets SILENT in K562 (TPM < 1.0) reach mean |z| 0.824 against 0.918 for expressed targets (p 5.2e-09) -- at or below the 0.859 floor set by 585 non-targeting guides, i.e. inert, which is what CRISPRi at an already-silent promoter should look like. HOW MUCH OF THAT IS NEW is a separate question and the answer is: not much that is demonstrable. Inside generic-abundance deciles the same contrast shrinks from 1.114x to 1.040x (0.857 vs 0.824) and reaches p<0.05 in only 35% of 20 draws of ~830 per arm, so most of what K562 expression knows about inert perturbations the generic table already knew, and the residual is not established at this n. WHAT IT DOES NOT BUY, WHICH IS THE PART THAT DECIDES WHETHER TO CARRY IT: the swap does not change a banked number. Re-matching the existing PPI layer's fast test with a third axis of measured-gene abundance moves the ratio from 1.1761 (two axes, 212,924 pairs) to 1.1720 with the generic table and 1.1697 with K562 RNA. Paired over 40 seeds -- the only way a difference smaller than either arm's draw-to-draw range is readable at all -- the K562 covariate absorbs more (-0.00236, signed-rank p 0.00019, more in 78% of individual draws), so the generic table was under-controlling in the predicted direction. The size of that under-control is 3.7% of PPI's 17.6% excess. That is real but small: PPI's ratio is not an abundance artefact under either covariate, and swapping them would not have changed a single admission decision this project has made. The better covariate is established; its consequence for this particular layer is not. Promoter accessibility adds nothing on top of the expression level: matched on K562 TPM decile, promoters open in all 4 ATAC experiments carry mean |z| 0.8962 against 0.9050 for promoters open in none (0.9904x over 20 draws) -- a ratio BELOW 1, i.e. if anything the accessible promoters are marginally less responsive, and the unmatched Spearman is -0.074. Accessibility is kept in the layer as state, not as a predictor. Finally, the prescribed pair fast test behaves exactly as predicted before it was run: 1.010x on 131,348 expression-defined pairs, because matching on perturbation strength removes a per-gene state layer by construction -- drop that one match and the same pairs give 1.113x. That is the size of what the test removes, and it is why this layer is scored as a covariate rather than against the 1.208x PPI reference."
}